## `kalshi_snapshots` — the underused table (found Aug 24)

15,027 rows, 72 days, 20 cities, Jun 13 – Aug 23. Columns: `snapshot_time, date,
city, bracket_label, yes_price_cents, no_price_cents, bracket_rank, sigma_p,
window_tz, window_label, utc_hour, model_top_bracket`.

**What it is:** exactly TWO snapshots per city-day — one EDGE, one CONVICTION,
1-2h apart depending on tz (ET 14/15 UTC, CT 14/16, PT 15/18, MT 16/18).
`bracket_rank` is the MARKET's price ranking (rank 1 avg 57.4¢ declining
monotonically to 1.5¢ at rank 6). Exactly 2,493 rows at each of ranks 1-6.

**What it can answer:** Edge→Conviction drift, bracket flip rates, model-vs-market
agreement, per-city bias, price-band P&L. All read-only, all freeze-safe.

**What it CANNOT answer:** intraday price evolution. There is no morning reading,
no late-afternoon reading, nothing near settlement. **The afternoon
near-certainty strategy ($0.85+ near-locked plays) happens AFTER the last capture
and cannot be evaluated from this table** — it needs new collection at later hours.

**Data hygiene:** ranks 7-12 are contamination (~40 rows vs 2,493, and rank 7
averages 13.5¢ against rank 6's 1.5¢ — structurally impossible in a price-sorted
ladder). Exclude `bracket_rank > 6` from all analysis.

